---
title: 12. Multiplayer (planned design; steps 1-2 built)
---
flowchart TB
    subgraph S1["Step 1: shared world and players (built: network.gd)"]
        direction LR
        host1["Host<br/>its saved world"] -->|"join: world settings<br/>+ edited chunks"| join1["Joining player<br/>generates the same world,<br/>applies the chunks, plays unsaved"]
        host1 <-->|"each player's position 20x a second<br/>(wrapped coordinates; the host relays)"| join1
    end

    subgraph S2["Step 2: shared sculpting (built: change tracking + network.gd)"]
        direction LR
        brush["Any tool, undo or redo<br/>applied at once locally"] -->|"every 0.1 s: the voxel values<br/>it changed (per chunk, compressed)"| owner2["Host (later: region owner)<br/>puts batches in one order"]
        owner2 -->|"ordered batch to everyone<br/>(the sender's comes back as a receipt)"| all2["Every computer applies them in order;<br/>own unconfirmed batches re-applied on top<br/>so all copies end up identical"]
    end

    subgraph S3["Step 3: shared physics"]
        direction LR
        rowner["Region owner simulates<br/>balls, frogs, objects in it"] -->|"body states"| others3["Everyone else<br/>shows them"]
        rowner -->|"body crosses border:<br/>hand it to the next owner"| next3["Neighbouring region owner"]
    end

    subgraph S4["Step 4: spreading the load"]
        direction LR
        dir["Directory<br/>(host; another takes over<br/>if it leaves)"] -->|"assign regions by load score<br/>(bodies + edits, per computer speed)<br/>prefer players nearby,<br/>move only past ~20% imbalance"| peers4["Each player's computer<br/>owns some of the 32x32 regions"]
    end

    subgraph S5["Step 5: finishing"]
        direction LR
        undo["Per-player undo<br/>(own strokes only)"] ~~~ save["Saving each region's edits"] ~~~ drop["Recovering when<br/>a player drops out"]
    end

    S1 --> S2 --> S3 --> S4 --> S5
